      #   we set above with the URL-extracted (encoded) form. Setting
      #   DATABASE_URL: "" here overrides the env_file value within the
      #   container so the entrypoint's `if [ -n ... ]` test fails and
      #   parse_url is skipped. DATABASE_URLS handled the same way.
      #   Verified against upstream entrypoint.sh source.
      DATABASE_URL: ""
      DATABASE_URLS: ""
````

Replace with:

````yaml
      # v2.49.7 — env_file dropped from this service entirely (see
      # comment above). DATABASE_URL no longer reaches the container,
      # so the entrypoint's parse_url branch never runs and DB_PASSWORD
      # set above is preserved verbatim.
````

Replace the leading comment block on the `environment:` block (the
one that starts "v2.49.5 — bypass DATABASE_URL parsing") with one
that captures the final state:

Find:

````yaml
    environment:
      # v2.49.5 — bypass DATABASE_URL parsing. The edoburu entrypoint
      # extracts the password from DATABASE_URL without URL-decoding it,
      # so URL-special chars (%, $, @, :) land in userlist.txt
      # URL-encoded while asyncpg and PG expect the decoded form. SCRAM
      # fails on both legs. Discrete DB_* env vars take raw strings.
      DB_HOST: hp1-postgres
      DB_PORT: "5432"
      DB_USER: ${POSTGRES_USER}
      DB_PASSWORD: ${POSTGRES_PASSWORD}
      DB_NAME: ${POSTGRES_DB:-hp1_agent}
````

Replace with:

````yaml
    environment:
      # v2.49.5–v2.49.7 — pgbouncer auth wiring.
      #
      # Why this looks the way it does:
      # 1. env_file is intentionally NOT set on this service. The
      #    edoburu entrypoint unconditionally runs parse_url against
      #    DATABASE_URL when non-empty, overwriting DB_PASSWORD with
      #    a URL-encoded substring. DATABASE_URL is required for
      #    hp1_agent so we can't remove it from .env, and compose
      #    issue #11740 prevents empty-string overrides on env_file
      #    inheritance. Solution: don't inherit env_file here.
      # 2. ${POSTGRES_USER} / ${POSTGRES_PASSWORD} interpolation still
      #    pulls values from the project-default .env file at
      #    docker/.env — that's a compose interpolation feature
      #    independent of env_file: directive on the service.
      # 3. AUTH_TYPE=scram-sha-256 makes the entrypoint write the
      #    password as plaintext to userlist.txt (its branch logic
      #    requires plain or scram-sha-256 for plaintext; trust falls
      #    through to md5, which PG14+ rejects).
      DB_HOST: hp1-postgres
      DB_PORT: "5432"
      DB_USER: ${POSTGRES_USER}
      DB_PASSWORD: ${POSTGRES_PASSWORD}
      DB_NAME: ${POSTGRES_DB:-hp1_agent}
````

(Lines below `DB_NAME` — the `# v2.49.6 ...` comment block plus the
two empty-string overrides — are removed by the prior edit. Keep the
rest of the block: `POOL_MODE`, `AUTH_TYPE`, `LISTEN_PORT`, etc.)

## Change 2 — `docker/PGBOUNCER.md`

Find the section "### 4. Two readers, two credential sources" and
its v2.49.6 trailing note:

````markdown
Note (v2.49.6): the pgbouncer service explicitly sets
`DATABASE_URL: ""` and `DATABASE_URLS: ""` in its compose `environment:`
block. This is required because the edoburu entrypoint
unconditionally re-parses `DATABASE_URL` (when non-empty) and
overwrites the discrete `DB_PASSWORD` we set with the URL-extracted
substring — which is URL-encoded and breaks SCRAM. Compose's
`environment:` overrides `env_file:` per-service, so this neutralises
the inherited value inside the container without affecting any other
service that needs `DATABASE_URL` (notably hp1_agent).
````

Replace with:

````markdown
Note (v2.49.7): the pgbouncer service does **not** set `env_file:` at
all. Compose interpolates `${POSTGRES_USER}` / `${POSTGRES_PASSWORD}`
from `docker/.env` via its standard project-default-env mechanism,
but does not bulk-import `.env` into the container.

This is required because the edoburu entrypoint unconditionally
re-parses `DATABASE_URL` when non-empty and overwrites the discrete
`DB_PASSWORD` with the URL-extracted (URL-encoded) substring,
breaking SCRAM. Compose's documented `environment` > `env_file`
precedence does **not** apply for empty/null values — empty-string
overrides fall through to env_file values
(github.com/docker/compose#11740, open since 2024). The only reliable
workaround is to not have env_file inherit `DATABASE_URL` into this
service at all.

Other services in the compose file that need `DATABASE_URL` (notably
hp1_agent) keep their `env_file: .env` and are unaffected.
````

