## Commit

````bash
git add -A
git commit -m "fix(infra): drop env_file from pgbouncer service (v2.49.7)

Empty-string overrides in compose 'environment:' do NOT actually
override env_file values (docker/compose#11740, open since 2024).
v2.49.6's DATABASE_URL: \"\" therefore had no effect: DATABASE_URL
remained populated in the pgbouncer container, the edoburu
entrypoint ran parse_url against it, and DB_PASSWORD got clobbered
with the URL-encoded substring — same SCRAM failure as before.

Verified by inspecting the running container env after v2.49.6
deploy: DATABASE_URL was non-empty despite the empty-string
override.

Fix: pgbouncer service no longer inherits env_file: .env. Compose
interpolates \${POSTGRES_USER}/\${POSTGRES_PASSWORD} from the
project-default .env file via its standard interpolation mechanism
(independent of the env_file: service key), so the values still
come from docker/.env — they just don't get bulk-imported into
the container.

Other services (notably hp1_agent) keep env_file: .env and are
unaffected."
git push origin main
````

## Deploy

After CC commits and CI image rebuild:

````bash
# On agent-01
cd /opt/hp1-agent
git pull origin main

# .env is unchanged — POSTGRES_PASSWORD with $$ stays
cd docker
docker compose --env-file .env --profile pgbouncer up -d --force-recreate pgbouncer

# Verify DATABASE_URL is no longer in the container env
docker exec hp1_pgbouncer env | grep -E '^(DATABASE_URL|DATABASE_URLS|DB_)'
# Should show ONLY DB_HOST, DB_PORT, DB_USER, DB_PASSWORD, DB_NAME.
# NO DATABASE_URL, NO DATABASE_URLS.

# Userlist should now have LITERAL password (no %25, no %24)
docker exec hp1_pgbouncer cat /etc/pgbouncer/userlist.txt

docker compose ps pgbouncer
# Expect (healthy)

# Real upstream auth — run inside the container shell to dodge any
# bash-quoting weirdness on the host
docker exec hp1_pgbouncer sh -c 'PGPASSWORD="${DB_PASSWORD}" psql -h /var/run/pgbouncer -p 6432 -U hp1 -d hp1_agent -c "SELECT 1;"'
````

If `SELECT 1;` returns one row, both SCRAM legs work. The next
operator step is to flip hp1_agent's `DATABASE_URL` to the socket
form and recreate hp1_agent.


